Z||000008||Boomtastic||07-26-2001||01:41 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KRMFiero:<BR><B>Josh, When do you think he will be attending NE Fiero shows? I want to see it    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Right now the rear end is torn apart as I install the Strange posi differential and back the gears down from Richmond 4.11's to 3.55's (better streetability!), and there's a LOT of undercarrige work (painting, running fuel & tranny lines, adding a drveshaft loop, etc.) that I want to do while the rear is in the air. More pictures are on the web site - <A HREF="http://www.boomtastic.com" TARGET=_blank>www.boomtastic.com</A>  (shameless plug   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) ......<p>[This message has been edited by Boomtastic (edited 07-26-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000009||88CoupeV6||07-27-2001||09:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Boomtastic:<BR><B> back the gears down from Richmond 4.11's to 3.55's (better streetability!)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Think of the fun mashing the gas with 4.11 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, then again I wouldn't want you to have an accident on the seats  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||12
Z||000010||Boomtastic||07-27-2001||02:32 PM||||The 4.11 gears (with this engine & cam) are WAAAAAAAY too steep for city driving. The RPM range would be through the roof. (It was approx. 3600 @ 60 MPH) As it is now, the stall convertor will give it enough *oomph* off the line.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||13
